![Figure A6. Conditional Prediction Loop](Figure_A6_Conditional_Prediction_Loop_v1.png)

Figure A.6. Conditional prediction loop depicting patterned regulatory responses following stabilization under constraint. Stabilized configurations participate in recurrent cycles involving environmental affordances and exposure, producing repeatable response patterns without implying inevitability, directionality, or terminal closure. Predictive reliability is contingent on the persistence of constraints and degrades when cost structures or environmental conditions shift, permitting re-routing without presuming resolution or fixed outcome.
